    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0386" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00113 E.W./10–2744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-27T17:00:00+01:00">October 27, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9261. Replying to the representations that we made to the Foreign Office on the
                    subject matter of paragraph 2 of Department’s 8689, October 12 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">19</hi>], Hall-Patch has informed us that the British
                    are willing to take part in talks on reparation and economic security. As
                    regards the date they are not quite ready but hope to be in a position to begin
                    in 2 or 3 weeks time. They assume that the timing will depend largely on the
                    sort of reply we receive from the Soviet. In this connection please note the
                    proposal in paragraph (1) of section IV of the memorandum on reparation and
                    economic security<anchor n="32" xml:id="d184-f1"/> which <pb facs="0387" n="373"
                        xml:id="pg373"/> Ambassador Winant has taken with him to Washington. Please
                    refer also to Embassy’s 9227, October 26.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
